# What never belongs in this repo.
#
# Not housekeeping — load-bearing. Onboarding step 1 runs `git add -A`, and
# the README tells you to run `pnpm install` and commit the lockfile it
# writes; both of those stage everything in the tree that git is not told to
# ignore. Without this file the first commit of a customer workspace carries
# node_modules/ and every app's build output.
#
# Both CI workflows already prune these same directory names when they walk
# the tree (.github/scripts/discover-apps.sh, and the compile floor check in
# validate.yaml), so this list and those prunes are two views of one rule:
# these directories are generated, and nothing here reads them as source.

# Dependencies. Restored by `pnpm install` from pnpm-lock.yaml, which IS
# committed.
node_modules/

# Build output. `out/` is oxyc publish's default outDir; `dist/` and `build/`
# are what a Vite or Next app writes when its oxy-app.json names one instead.
out/
dist/
build/

# The oxy CLI's local state directory.
.oxy_state/

# Local secrets. Credentials for pipelines and apps belong in the platform's
# secret manager, never in a file in this repo — an ignored .env is where
# people put them anyway, so make sure an accident stays local.
.env*

.DS_Store
